nd its amplitude (height) increases.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APropagation_du_tsunami_en_profondeur_variable.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Tsunami2.JPG/500px-Tsunami2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Tsunami2.JPG/500px-Tsunami2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The wave further slows and amplifies as it hits land. Only the largest waves crest.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATsunami2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Shallow_water_wave.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Shallow_water_wave.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An illustration of the rhythmic \"drawback\" of surface water associated with a wave.  It follows that a very large drawback may herald the arrival of a very large wave.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShallow_water_wave.gif"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/Tsunami_run-up%2C_height%2C_and_inundation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/Tsunami_run-up%2C_height%2C_and_inundation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Diagram showing several measures to describe a tsunami size, including height, inundation and run-up","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATsunami_run-up%2C_height%2C_and_inundation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Bamfield_Tsunami_Hazard_Zone_sign.jpg/250px-Bamfield_Tsunami_Hazard_Zone_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t